    "summary": "- API keys are stored only as SHA-256 hashes plus `last4`. Tokens are `tly_` + 40 chars from crypto/rand, returned once on create and invite-accept, and absent from GET, snapshots and logs.\n- Auth hashes the presented token. Revoked keys and removed members still get 401. Legacy plain-text snapshot tokens still load and are rewritten hashed on the next save. `last_used_at` is written at most once per minute per key.\n- `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` pass, with new tests covering format, hashing, legacy migration, the no-plaintext snapshot check, and the throttle.",
